terms.acceptance.title: 1. Acceptance of Terms
terms.acceptance.p1: By accessing or using the UniSearch website and related tools, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to these Terms of Use. If you do not agree, please discontinue using the service.
terms.purpose.title: 2. Scope & Service Purpose
terms.purpose.p1: UniSearch is an independent academic discovery and search workspace built to help prospective students research undergraduate programs, entrance requirements, tuition rates, and funding options.
terms.purpose.p2: The catalog is strictly focused on undergraduate studies and aggregates officially published institutional data.
terms.disclaimer.title: 3. Informational Nature & Educational Disclaimer
terms.disclaimer.callout: Notice: UniSearch is not an admissions office and is not officially affiliated with the universities listed. Algorithmic scores are preliminary estimates and do not guarantee admission.
terms.disclaimer.educational_status: UniSearch is an independent, non-commercial research initiative developed by high school students as an applied educational endeavor. The service is not an official admissions office, accredited governmental body, or formal admissions agency.
terms.disclaimer.as_is: All services, algorithmic models (UniFit, UniChance), and catalog listings are provided strictly on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis without warranties of any kind. While we strive for data freshness, requirements can shift. Users bear sole responsibility for verifying final criteria directly on official university portals.
terms.disclaimer.p1: All information presented on this platform (exam thresholds, minimum scores, application deadlines, tuition costs, and scholarships) is provided for general guidance only.
terms.disclaimer.p2: UniFit (smart sorting) and UniChance (admission chance estimation) are algorithmic guides. They cannot and do not guarantee university acceptance, student visa grants, or financial aid awards.
terms.disclaimer.p3: Universities may revise admission criteria, tuition rates, and application timelines without prior notice. Applicants bear sole responsibility for verifying final requirements directly on official university portals.
terms.disclaimer.p4: UniSearch assumes no liability for admissions committee outcomes, missed application deadlines, or financial expenditures incurred by users.
terms.accounts.title: 4. User Accounts & Security
terms.accounts.p1: For convenient synchronization of profile metrics and bookmarks across devices, UniSearch may offer sign-in via third-party providers (including Google Sign-In). This functionality is currently in development.
terms.accounts.p2: Users agree not to access accounts belonging to other individuals without authorization and remain responsible for maintaining access security on their personal devices.
terms.ip.title: 5. Intellectual Property & Fair Use
terms.ip.non_affiliation: UniSearch is an independent catalog and is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by any universities listed on the platform. All university names, crests, logos, and trademarks belong to their respective owners and are used strictly for informational reference (Nominative Fair Use).
terms.ip.p1: University names, crests, and official emblems remain the trademarks of their respective academic institutions, and campus photographs remain the property of their respective photographers and institutions. They are utilized in UniSearch strictly for identification and non-commercial educational purposes under the fair use doctrine.
terms.ip.p2: Platform application source code, interface designs, layout architecture, and proprietary algorithms belong to the creators of UniSearch.
terms.ip.takedown: Notice & Takedown Procedure: if you are an authorized university representative, photographer/copyright holder of any image, or intellectual property owner and wish to request attribution credit, adjustment, or removal of any logo, photograph, or institutional reference, please notify us at unisearch@inbox.ru. We will review and address the request within 48 hours.
terms.acceptable_use.title: 6. Acceptable Use Policy
terms.acceptable_use.p1: When accessing or utilizing the platform, users agree not to engage in prohibited activities:
terms.acceptable_use.li1: Attempting unauthorized access to server infrastructure or circumventing security controls.
terms.acceptable_use.li2: Denial-of-service attempts, excessive request spamming, or aggressive automated scraping that bypasses API rate limit headers.
terms.acceptable_use.li3: Using the service to transmit malware, malicious code, or unsolicited communications.
terms.third_party.title: 7. Third-Party External Links
terms.third_party.p1: UniSearch links to external university websites, application gateways, and educational resources. We do not manage external content or privacy policies and bear no responsibility for their operations.
